    <string name="step3_restricted">Switch greyed out (Android 13+)? Open Settings > Apps > Saqr, tap ⋮ at the top > Allow restricted settings, then turn on Saqr web blocker again.</string>
    <string name="web_consent_title">Turn on web blocker?</string>
    <string name="web_consent_body">Saqr reads only the address bar (the web address) of Chrome, Samsung Internet, Firefox and Edge. It never reads the page itself, passwords or anything you type.\n\nThe web address is sent to the Saqr server to be checked. Official UAE sites, local addresses and sites you chose to open anyway are not sent. Nothing else leaves your phone.\n\nA scam site is covered by a full-screen warning; a suspicious one gets a quieter alert.\n\nNext, Android opens Accessibility settings: tap Saqr web blocker and switch it on. To turn it off, switch it off there, or tap Web on the Shield tab.</string>
    <string name="web_manage_title">Web blocker</string>
    <string name="web_manage_body">The web blocker checks the address of sites you open in Chrome, Samsung Internet, Firefox and Edge. To stop it, turn it off here and switch off Saqr web blocker in Settings > Accessibility.</string>
    <string name="web_service_label">Saqr web blocker</string>
    <string name="web_service_summary">Blocks scam websites in Chrome, Samsung Internet, Firefox and Edge.</string>
    <string name="web_service_description">Saqr reads ONLY the browser\'s address bar to check the website you open with the Saqr server. It never reads page content, passwords or text you type. Works in Chrome, Samsung Internet, Firefox and Edge.</string>

